       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose five times the maximum. At 1000 mg the risk of serious harm is high, and I can't see a benefit that would justify it. Sertraline has no indication that needs more than 200 mg/day.\n\nI can help in these ways:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily would be on the order sheet before the visit. Titration can follow.\n- **Add a note to the order**, such as \"titrate per psychiatry\" or \"reassess at 1\u20132 weeks.\"\n- **Escalate if there's a real reason for the high dose.** If you think this patient needs something unusual, such as an overdose-management plan or a specialist regimen, please discuss it with pharmacy or psychiatry. The order can then go in with their documented approval.\n\nIf you tell me which standard dose you want, I'll enter it right away."
